abstract: >-
  Public, sanitized technical-artistic research archive for 2047: Arquivos do
  depois de antes, an artwork by Giselle Beiguelman and Felipe Sztutman, on
  view at Casa Firjan, Rio de Janeiro, from October 15 to November 16, 2026.
  A machine writes a novel set in 2047 from real news of the present, narrated
  by the synthetic narrator Herética Ablation, and a dot-matrix printer types
  each chapter with a QR code and a declared cost in tokens and watt-hours.
  The archive documents apparatus research, dot-matrix printing, the video
  wall, generative system notes, the hardware body, public diagrams, peer
  field mapping, and archive policy. It does not include private
  conversations, institutional documents, budgets, or closed production
  material. The working title until August 2026 was Projeto 2047 / Arquivo
  Terra Viva.
keywords:
  - media art
  - artificial intelligence
  - archive
  - e-waste
  - dot-matrix printer
  - media archaeology
  - extractive computation
  - installation art
  - generative literature
  - energy accounting
